/// The depth limit is an `Error` like every VM error, caught by
/// `on: Error do:`: its `signal` runs in a reserve above the limit
/// (docs/design/execution.md, "The depth limit"). The second recursion is
/// caught the same way, because the reserve is given back once the first
/// signal is over: were it not, the second would overrun it. That the
/// error is an instance of `Error` itself, no subclass,
/// `crates/ns-runtime/tests/representation.rs` checks.
class TheDepthLimitIsCaught = Object new () (
  recurse = (
    ^self recurse.
  )

  public main: platform args: arguments = (
    |
      transcript = platform transcript.
    |
    transcript
        show: ([self recurse] on: Error do: [:e | e messageText]);
        newLine.
    transcript
        show: ([self recurse] on: Error do: [:error | 'Error']);
        newLine.
    transcript
        show: 'done';
        newLine.
  )
)
